    "result_text": "The full test suite is green \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**, 21 tests, 0 failures/errors (the acceptance package is the entire test suite).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `sharesHousehold` / `householdId` behaviour for `POST /api/owners`. The endpoint already allowed a same-lastName-same-address owner through when `sharesHousehold: true` (via `CheckOwnerHouseholdUnique`); what was missing was assigning and returning a shared `householdId`.\n\nChanges:\n\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `householdId` field (`household_id` column) with getter/setter, mirroring the existing `customerCode`.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `householdId` as a read-only string on the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field and MapStruct maps it into `GET` responses automatically.\n- **`rest/function/owner/AssignHouseholdId.java`** (new) \u2014 when `sharesHousehold` is true, derives a **stable** 12-char hex id deterministically from the normalized last name + address (same normalization as the uniqueness check), assigns it to the new owner, and **back-fills the same id onto the existing household member(s)** so both sides match.\n- **`officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted an `assignHousehold` step (under `transaction` governance) between `build` and `assignCode`.\n- **DB schemas** \u2014 added the `household_id` column to hsqldb (used by tests), h2, mysql, postgres, and appended a trailing `NULL` to the positional owner seed inserts in hsqldb/mysql so the column counts still match.\n\nThe determinism guarantees that two owners created into the same household (same last name + address) receive an identical, non-blank `householdId` regardless of creation order \u2014 exactly what `Cp11Tests.coreJoinersShareHouseholdId` asserts \u2014 while `Cp10`'s conflict/allow behaviour is unchanged.",
